\ Not supported yet (136): ¬ (a = b) is a function type through whnfD,
\ not an inductive type (Lean: "Tactic `rcases` failed: `h : a = b →
\ False` is not an inductive datatype", RCases.lean:309; LeanForth's
\ 471), but the message's type is a binder whose kind the declaration's
\ type does not give (plan S5), so the run stops unsupported, never
\ accepted. test.fs reaches 471 with a type it can print.
theorem x_not_inductive
  Nat explicit: a  Nat explicit: b
  a b = ¬ explicit: h
  a a =
:= by
  ' h by-rcases[ << x y >> ]
  by-rfl
end x_not_inductive
